# Copy to .dev.vars (gitignored). In production BOTH of these are secrets
# (`cd cloud/worker && npx wrangler secret put SESSION_SECRET` / `… ROSTER`) —
# never values in wrangler.toml, and never committed.

# The HMAC key the login app signs its sess cookie with (src/auth.ts verifies,
# never mints). Any value works for `wrangler dev` and the smoke test; to accept
# REAL sessions it must equal the login app's own SESSION_SECRET byte for byte.
SESSION_SECRET=dev-secret-change-me

# AUTHORIZATION: which authenticated email owns which tenant store, as one line
# of JSON (email → {uid, active}). `active: false` is the revocation lever — the
# entry stays, the cookie keeps verifying, and every request 403s. An email
# absent here is authenticated-but-unauthorized, exactly the same answer.
#
# uids must match /^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,31}$/ (they name the store prefix
# u/<uid>/); a row that does not is dropped at parse. Malformed rows are dropped
# too, and an unparseable value authorizes NOBODY rather than falling back.
ROSTER={"you@example.com":{"uid":"t1","active":true},"someone-else@example.com":{"uid":"t2","active":true}}

# --- the reader worker (wrangler.reader.toml, src/reader.ts) -----------------
# All four are `wrangler secret put …` in production. They live here for
# `npx wrangler dev -c wrangler.reader.toml`, which reads this same file.
#
# The issuer to PIN. Every endpoint is read from the discovery document beneath
# it, so this is the only IdP address in the configuration — note it carries a
# TENANT PATH, while the logout page src/oidc.ts links is at the issuer's ORIGIN.
OIDC_ISSUER=https://auth.example.com/t/your-tenant

# This application's registered client_id, and the secret it authenticates the
# token exchange with (client_secret_basic). Register the client at the IdP with
# redirect_uri EXACTLY `https://<this worker's host>/auth/callback` — the
# comparison there is un-normalized on purpose, so a trailing slash is a
# different URI and sign-in stops at the IdP with "misconfigured application".
OIDC_CLIENT_ID=srr
OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=dev-client-secret-change-me

# The key this worker signs its OWN session cookie with (session.ts) — unrelated
# to the IdP, and never shared with anything. Rotating it signs everybody out,
# which is the intended emergency lever. Any value works locally.
SESSION_HMAC_SECRET=dev-session-hmac-change-me
